-- title:
--   Schedule identities for restart bit coverage
-- statement:
--   For a rational number $\rho$ and an annealing schedule $s$, this bundle defines two auxiliary predicates. The first fixes the schedule's cooling factor; the second fixes its draw-call allowance:
--   $$\operatorname{RhoProperty}(\rho,s)\iff s.\rho=\rho,\qquad
--   \operatorname{DrawCallsProperty}(s)\iff D=3L(A+N).$$
--   Here $L=s.L$ is the phase count, $A=s.\mathrm{restartCap}$ is the restart cap, $N=s.\mathrm{observations}$ is the observation count, and $D=s.\mathrm{drawCalls}$ is the scheduled draw allowance. These are identities of schedule fields, with no positivity or tape-coverage assertion built into the predicates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartPhaseBitCoverage.lean#L24-L25

